  dishName: Adobo
  dishSprite: {fileID: 0}
  pages:
  - Wonderful work. The sauce in your pan is a map of three centuries of culinary
    exchange.
  - Mexican tomato, Spanish sofrito technique, Chinese soy sauce, Filipino calamansi,
  - ' all balanced against each other in the Kapampangan Sunday dinner tradition.'
  - The Spanish word for roasting stayed, but the method became braising to suit
    a tropical kitchen.
  - but as a slow weaving of ingredients and techniques into something new that neither
    parent cuisine would quite recognize.
